Added API consumption accounting for token-authenticated REST and GraphQL requests, configured via the new `RATE_LIMITING` setting: each request is assigned a cost computed from its shape alone and recorded against a per-token budget in Redis, and in `report` mode every response carries `X-Nautobot-Cost` and `RateLimit-*` headers without ever denying a request.
Added consumption budget enforcement (`RATE_LIMITING["MODE"] = "enforce"`): once a token's recorded consumption reaches the configured limit, further requests receive an immediate 429 with `Retry-After` before any database work is performed. Mode may also be set per request kind — for example enforcing REST while GraphQL remains in report mode.
Added an optional consumption calibration log (`RATE_LIMITING["CALIBRATION_LOG"]`) that emits one structured JSON record per request, pairing the assigned cost and its heuristic inputs with measured wall-clock, CPU, and database time — the offline dataset for tuning the cost heuristic weights before enabling enforcement.
